# Auto Claude UI - Browser Live Mode Configuration
# =================================================
# These environment variables are used when running the UI in browser mode
# with a live FastAPI backend (pnpm run dev:browser:live)

# API Server URL (HTTP endpoints)
VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:8766

# WebSocket Server URL (real-time events)
VITE_WS_URL=ws://localhost:8766

# ============================================
# USAGE NOTES
# ============================================
#
# Three Development Modes:
#
# 1. Electron Mode (IPC) - Default
#    Command: pnpm run dev
#    Backend: IPC communication to Python backend
#    Port: N/A (uses IPC channels)
#
# 2. Browser Mode (Mock) - Offline UI Development
#    Command: pnpm run dev:browser
#    Backend: Mocked APIs (fake data)
#    Port: http://localhost:5173
#
# 3. Browser Mode (Live API) - Full-stack without Electron
#    Command: pnpm run dev:browser:live
#    Backend: Real FastAPI server
#    Ports: http://localhost:5173 (UI), http://localhost:8766 (API)
#
# The browser-mock.ts file automatically detects which mode to use:
#   1. Check if window.electronAPI exists → Use Electron IPC
#   2. Try HTTP health check at VITE_API_URL → Use HTTP client
#   3. Fall back to mocks → Use browser mocks
